 "char": {
  "id": "hal",
  "handle": "hal_and_his_bulbs",
  "name": "Hal",
  "bio": "I collect old lightbulbs. Stay with me.",
  "voice": "bm_george",
  "case": "phoebus",
  "look": {
   "skin": "#e6bc9c",
   "hair": "#e8e4dc",
   "style": "side",
   "shirt": "#8a6a2a",
   "glasses": true,
   "extra": "moustache"
  },
  "script": "I collect old lightbulbs. Sounds dull. Stay with me. In 1924 the biggest bulb makers in the world, including Osram and Philips, formed a cartel called Phoebus. They agreed a bulb should last a thousand hours, down from about two and a half thousand. And they fined each other if bulbs lasted too long. Meanwhile, a bulb in a fire station in Livermore, California, has been glowing since 1901. They don't make them like that anymore. For a while, that was on purpose."
 },
